e the reddit question  and answer that I did just an hour  before this and she had a question there  that didn't get answered so she's asking  it here which is fine she's asking you a  question so if you were going  to talk about the main idea in your new  book that puts these ideas together she  listened number of them but if you put  these ideas together from physics to  human reflection what would it be and  this is actually a question shell I  don't know if you stayed around to the  end of the read I sort of did discuss  this a little bit at the end but I'm  happy to do it here in this different  context look you know I don't think that  we're going to find purpose and meaning  written into the fundamental laws of  physics I don't think that within the  equations of general relativity or  quantum mechanics or whatever the future  laws of physics that we discover maybe I  don't think you're ever gonna find a  place in which you're gonna say aha  there is the reason why we humans are  here there is the purpose of life I just  don't think that the universe is built  that way we are collections of particles  governed by those physical laws and it  just so happens that for a brief period  of time the ingredients come together to  yield conscious beings like ourselves  and conscious beings can begin to  question reality and begin to wonder  about where we came from and begin to  wonder why we are here and that's just a  natural outgrowth of the evolving nature  of complex particulate arrangements at  least some of those arrangements that  take place on planet Earth so my view is  you don't look to physics in that sense  for that kind of flat-footed  straightforward directive as to what  meaning and purpose there is in the  universe rather you look to physics to  understand the framework the context  within which living beings such as  ourselves exist and within that as I  described in the book this guy over here  within that you can find a certain kind  of gratificati